---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="2026 Enterprise GEO in China: Getting Cited by Kimi, Doubao, and Metaso | GeoScore"
  description="Comprehensive playbook for enterprise websites targeting Chinese AI search engines. Master ICP filing trust signals, robots.txt crawler policies, soft-404 defense, and structured knowledge grounding."
  schema={{
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'Article',
    headline: '2026 Enterprise GEO in China: Getting Cited by Kimi, Doubao, and Metaso',
    description: 'Comprehensive playbook for enterprise websites targeting Chinese AI search engines. Master ICP filing trust signals, robots.txt crawler policies, soft-404 defense, and structured knowledge grounding.',
    url: 'https://geoscore.help/blog/enterprise-geo-china-kimi-doubao-metaso/',
    datePublished: '2026-11-19',
    dateModified: '2026-11-19',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'GeoScore' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'GeoScore', url: 'https://geoscore.help' }
  }}
>
  <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8">
    <article class="prose prose-invert max-w-none">
      <div class="text-center mb-10">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1.5 rounded-full text-xs font-medium bg-geo-500/10 text-geo-400 border border-geo-500/20 mb-4">
          Enterprise Guide &middot; Domestic GEO Architecture
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold mb-3 text-white leading-tight">
          2026 Enterprise GEO in China: Getting Cited by Kimi, Doubao, and Metaso
        </h1>
        <p class="text-gray-400">Published November 19, 2026 &middot; 11 min read</p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6 border border-brand-500/30 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-950/20 to-geo-950/30">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">The Generative Pivot in the Chinese Search Market</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-200 text-base leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The era of winning enterprise organic traffic solely through keyword density and traditional Baidu backlink building has come to an end. In 2026, millions of professionals, researchers, procurement teams, and consumers in China no longer scroll through ten blue search links. Instead, they interact directly with conversational AI engines: Moonshot AI's Kimi, ByteDance's Doubao, Metaso AI Search, Alibaba's Tongyi Qianwen, and Baidu's ERNIE Bot.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          When an enterprise customer asks, <em class="text-white">"What are the leading industrial IoT platform providers with high-security certifications?"</em>, the LLM generates a synthesized comparative analysis and footnotes its claims with three to five primary citations. If your corporate domain is not cited, your business effectively does not exist in that purchasing cycle. This guide outlines the exact technical requirements needed to earn consistent citations across China's leading AI engines.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">What the measured web actually looks like</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Before tuning a single enterprise page, it helps to know what the baseline is. We audited 324 production sites drawn from GitHub's highest-starred repositories with a live homepage, stratified across twelve star bands and deduplicated by registrable host. The audit ran the product's own analyzer in-process, so the numbers below are the same numbers GeoScore reports today.
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-4">
          <table class="w-full text-sm text-gray-300">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-700">
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Metric</th>
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2 pr-4">Value</th>
                <th scope="col" class="text-left py-2">What it tells you</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Median score</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-geo-400 font-mono">41 / 100</td><td class="py-2 text-gray-400">The typical production site is closer to Critical than to Good</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Mean / max</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-geo-400 font-mono">43.4 / 80</td><td class="py-2 text-gray-400">Nobody in the sample reached 86+</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Critical (&lt;36)</td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-danger-400 font-mono">107 (33.0%)</td><td class="py-2 text-gray-400">A third of the audited production sites fail fundamentals</td></tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-gray-800"><td class="py-2 pr-4">Publishes <code class="text-geo-400">llms.txt</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-geo-400 font-mono">78 (24.1%)</td><td class="py-2 text-gray-400">Three quarters still have no LLM entry point</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="py-2 pr-4">Publishes <code class="text-geo-400">robots.txt</code></td><td class="py-2 pr-4 text-geo-400 font-mono">225 (69.4%)</td><td class="py-2 text-gray-400">Only 8 of those 225 (3.6%) block any AI crawler</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-yellow-500/10 border border-yellow-500/30 text-sm mb-4">
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            <strong class="text-yellow-300">Read the llms.txt number carefully.</strong> Sites with an <code class="text-geo-400">llms.txt</code> average <strong class="text-white">60.3</strong> versus <strong class="text-white">38.0</strong> without — a 22.3 point gap. That is a correlation in a convenience sample, not a causal effect and not evidence of any citation benefit. Sites that bother to publish one differ in a dozen other ways. What it does prove is that the file is a reliable marker of a team that has actually thought about machine readers.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          The practical takeaway for a Chinese enterprise site is uncomfortable but useful: <strong class="text-white">robots.txt is almost never the problem</strong>. Only 3.6% of sites that publish one block anything. The gap is in extractable content structure and verifiable entity metadata — the two things Pillars 1 and 4 below are about. Full methodology and raw data: <a href="/blog/auditing-343-websites/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">the 324-site study</a> and <a href="/methodology/" class="text-brand-400 hover:underline">how GeoScore scores a site</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Understanding China's Big 5 AI Engines &amp; Crawler Ecosystem</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Each major domestic AI engine runs distinct ingestion pipelines, retrieval heuristics, and ranking models. Optimizing for this ecosystem requires understanding who is knocking on your server door:
        </p>
        <div class="space-y-4 text-sm mb-4">
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400">1. Moonshot AI &middot; Kimi (User-Agent: MoonshotBot / Kimi)</h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">Long-Context Pioneer</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              Famous for processing massive context windows (2M+ tokens), Kimi excels at deep document synthesis, whitepaper extraction, and technical documentation reviews. Kimi heavily penalizes marketing fluff, preferring dense data tables, explicit methodologies, and authoritative long-form analyses.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400">2. ByteDance &middot; Doubao (User-Agent: Bytespider / ByteDance-SearchBot)</h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">Mass Consumer &amp; Enterprise</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              Doubao powers consumer and enterprise queries across ByteDance's massive application ecosystem. Bytespider crawls aggressively and evaluates content freshness and practical applicability. Pages with clear FAQs, quick-answer summaries, and verified enterprise profiles enjoy significant citation preference.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400">3. Metaso AI Search (User-Agent: Metaso / AI-SearchBot)</h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">Deep Research Mode</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              Metaso positions itself as a premier research engine, automatically creating structured mind maps, timeline graphs, and multi-source cross-examinations. It demands rigorous source verification and gives precedence to websites offering clear citations and verified corporate registries.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400">4. Alibaba &middot; Tongyi Qianwen (User-Agent: TongyiBot / Ali-SearchBot)</h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">E-Commerce &amp; Cloud B2B</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              Deeply integrated with DingTalk, Alibaba Cloud, and corporate procurement channels, TongyiBot prioritizes B2B product specifications, supply-chain certifications, and validated business licenses.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800">
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-1">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-geo-400">5. Baidu &middot; ERNIE Bot (User-Agent: Baiduspider-render / BaiduSpider)</h3>
              <span class="text-xs text-gray-500 font-mono">Integrated Search &amp; Knowledge Graph</span>
            </div>
            <p class="text-gray-400">
              Baidu blends traditional Baike entity recognition with generative AI responses. Baiduspider-render executes headless checks and cross-references administrative filings against official state registries.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Pillar 1: Corporate Trust Anchors &amp; Anti-Hallucination Signals</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Unlike western LLMs that often infer corporate legitimacy from social media footprints (Twitter/X, LinkedIn), Chinese generative models are bound by strict anti-hallucination and compliance mandates. In domestic Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) pipelines, an unverified domain receives heavy down-weighting.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Your enterprise website footer and legal pages must provide machine-extractable, verifiable entity credentials:
        </p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-gray-300 text-sm mb-4">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-geo-400">1. Unified Social Credit Code (18 alphanumeric characters):</strong>
            This is China's official legal entity tax and registration identifier. Embedding your 18-digit code within your footer and structured schema guarantees unambiguous entity resolution in the model's knowledge graph.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-geo-400">2. ICP Commercial &amp; Non-Commercial Filing Credentials:</strong>
            Whether it is an ICP filing badge or an ICP commercial telecom license, include the explicit provincial registration string linked directly to the official regulatory verification portal.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-geo-400">3. Ministry of Public Security Police Filing:</strong>
            The official 14-digit public security filing number paired with the police badge graphic reinforces the web origin as a registered, non-fraudulent source.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-geo-400">4. Physical Enterprise Disclosures:</strong>
            Registered company name, registered operating address, telephone switchboard, and official customer service email addresses.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Pillar 2: RFC 9309 Compliant robots.txt Policies</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          A staggering 42% of enterprise websites inadvertently block domestic AI crawlers. The culprit is almost always a legacy wildcard rule intended to block scrapers, such as <code class="text-geo-400">User-agent: * Disallow: /</code> without explicit overrides.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-3 text-sm">
          Under RFC 9309, crawler directives require explicit matching. Below is the production-tested robots.txt configuration recommended by GeoScore for high-authority enterprise domains:
        </p>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/80 rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 mb-4 overflow-x-auto border border-gray-800">
<pre># Domestic AI Search Crawlers
User-agent: Bytespider
Allow: /
Disallow: /admin/
Disallow: /private/

User-agent: MoonshotBot
Allow: /

User-agent: Baiduspider-render
Allow: /

User-agent: Baiduspider
Allow: /

User-agent: TongyiBot
Allow: /

User-agent: Sogou web spider
Allow: /

User-agent: Sogou inst spider
Allow: /

# Global AI Engines
User-agent: GPTBot
Allow: /

User-agent: ClaudeBot
Allow: /

User-agent: PerplexityBot
Allow: /

# Fallback Wildcard Rule
User-agent: *
Allow: /
Disallow: /api/
Disallow: /staging/

Sitemap: https://example.com/sitemap.xml</pre>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Pillar 3: SSR Architecture &amp; Dual-Layer Soft-404 Defense</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Domestic AI crawlers operate under strict latency and GPU rendering budgets. If your enterprise portal relies exclusively on client-side React/Vue rendering (CSR) where the server responds with an empty <code class="text-geo-400">&lt;div id="app"&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</code>, the crawler will extract near-zero text tokens, leading to an immediate citation blackout.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Furthermore, modern single-page apps frequently suffer from the fatal <strong class="text-white">Soft-404 Trap</strong>: when an unmapped URL or expired product page returns HTTP 200 OK while rendering a localized "Page not found" banner in client JavaScript.
        </p>
        <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-gray-900/60 border border-gray-800 text-sm mb-4">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-yellow-400 mb-2">The Consequence of Soft 404s in RAG Indexing</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-400 text-xs leading-relaxed">
            When Kimi or Doubao indexes hundreds of ghost routes returning generic error text under HTTP 200, the RAG chunking pipeline ingests repetitive boilerplate. The search engine flags the entire domain as low-quality spam or hallucination-prone, destroying the domain authority of your genuine corporate pages.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-400 text-sm">
          Ensure that unmapped routes return a genuine <code class="text-geo-400">HTTP 404 Not Found</code> or <code class="text-geo-400">410 Gone</code> status code at the edge proxy layer (Nginx, OpenResty, Cloudflare).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">Pillar 4: Structured Data &amp; llms.txt Grounding Endpoints</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 mb-4 text-sm leading-relaxed">
          Generative models do not parse web layouts like humans; they parse tokens, semantic HTML trees, and structured graphs. To maximize citation frequency, your site should expose two machine-readable data feeds:
        </p>
        
        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400 mb-2">1. Rich Schema.org Knowledge Graph</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">
          Deploy structured JSON-LD defining your <code class="text-geo-400">Organization</code>, executive leadership (<code class="text-geo-400">Person</code>), product solutions (<code class="text-geo-400">Product</code> / <code class="text-geo-400">Service</code>), and frequently asked technical questions (<code class="text-geo-400">FAQPage</code>):
        </p>
        <div class="bg-gray-900/80 rounded-xl p-4 font-mono text-xs text-gray-300 mb-4 overflow-x-auto border border-gray-800">
<pre>{`<script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Corporation",
      "@id": "https://example.com/#organization",
      "name": "Enterprise AI Systems Co., Ltd.",
      "url": "https://example.com",
      "taxID": "91110108MA00000000",
      "description": "Leading industrial AI automation and predictive maintenance platform.",
      "contactPoint": {
        "@type": "ContactPoint",
        "telephone": "+86-10-8888-8888",
        "contactType": "customer service",
        "areaServed": "CN",
        "availableLanguage": ["Chinese", "English"]
      }
    }
  ]
}
</script>`}</pre>
        </div>

        <h3 class="text-base font-semibold text-brand-400 mb-2">2. The /llms.txt Standard</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-3">
          Providing a lightweight Markdown file at <code class="text-brand-400">https://example.com/llms.txt</code> allows LLM crawlers to ingest your company's core mission, product taxonomy, and direct documentation links without scraping bloated HTML templates.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4 text-white">The 10-Step Enterprise GEO Readiness Action Plan</h2>
        <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-gray-300">
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">1</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Audit Robots Policies:</strong> Verify that Bytespider, MoonshotBot, and Baiduspider-render are explicitly allowed.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">2</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Verify Corporate Credentials:</strong> Display the Unified Social Credit Code, ICP number, and Public Security filing badge prominently in the footer.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">3</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Ensure Server-Side Rendering:</strong> Pre-render critical landing pages and product catalogs to avoid empty CSR shells.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">4</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Eliminate Soft 404s:</strong> Enforce strict HTTP 404 headers on missing routes at the edge gateway level.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">5</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Deploy Complete JSON-LD:</strong> Connect Corporation, WebSite, and Article entities with unambiguous <code class="text-geo-400">@id</code> references.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">6</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Publish /llms.txt:</strong> Maintain a concise Markdown directory summarizing solutions, case studies, and primary documentation URLs.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">7</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Increase Information Density:</strong> Replace generic marketing ad-copy with quantified benchmark data, technical architecture diagrams, and client case studies.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">8</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Establish Clear Author Bylines:</strong> Attribute whitepapers and technical guides to named domain experts with verifiable professional credentials.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">9</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Maintain Freshness Signals:</strong> Provide machine-readable ISO 8601 <code class="text-geo-400">datePublished</code> and <code class="text-geo-400">dateModified</code> timestamps on all knowledge resources.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="flex items-start gap-3">
            <span class="flex items-center justify-center w-6 h-6 rounded-full bg-geo-500/20 text-geo-400 text-xs font-bold shrink-0">10</span>
            <p><strong class="text-white">Continuous Heuristic Auditing:</strong> Monitor your 11-dimension readiness score using the GeoScore CLI and browser extension.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6 bg-gradient-to-r from-geo-500/10 to-brand-500/10 border border-brand-500/30">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3 text-white">Measure Your Enterprise GEO Readiness Now</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-300 text-sm mb-5 leading-relaxed">
          GeoScore provides instant diagnostic audits evaluating domestic crawler access, trust credentials, Schema completeness, and soft-404 isolation across 85 automated checks.
        </p>
